{
  "tickets": [
    {
      "id": "gen-351",
      "subject": "Pharmacy refill substitution workflow help",
      "body": "We need to know the proper steps for handling pharmacy notifications when a prescribed medication is out of stock. Several of our doctors are trying to figure out how to switch the prescription to an alternative without having to rebuild the order from scratch. Please provide the workflow documentation for these substitution messages."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-352",
      "subject": "Clearinghouse validation errors on batch claims",
      "body": "We keep getting validation errors when trying to generate and batch our insurance claims for electronic submission. Can you tell us how to clear these out so we can get our daily batches sent over to the clearinghouse?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-353",
      "subject": "Password resets and security policy lockouts",
      "body": "This is the third time this week I've had to deal with locked accounts because of these overly aggressive password rules. How do I adjust the security policies so staff aren't constantly getting locked out, and where is the simple button to reset their credentials without jumping through hoops?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-354",
      "subject": "Questions regarding automated text reminder delivery timing",
      "body": "Hello, I am hoping to get some guidance on how our automated appointment reminders are sent out. A few patients mentioned they haven't been receiving their SMS notifications recently, and I would like to check our settings to make sure everything is configured properly. Could you let me know where I can review the delivery logs and adjust the reminder timing?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-355",
      "subject": "Inquiry regarding medication out-of-stock notification procedures",
      "body": "Good afternoon. Our clinical staff are currently reviewing our internal protocols for handling pharmacy notices when prescribed items are unavailable. Could you please provide guidance on the standard messaging workflow for managing therapeutic substitutions within the system? We want to ensure our providers are utilizing the correct pathways for these updates."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-356",
      "subject": "Updating closed pharmacy in directory",
      "body": "So sorry to bother you with this, but one of our patients' regular pharmacies just closed down. Could you quickly remind me how to search the directory for their new location and save it to their profile? Thanks!"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-357",
      "subject": "Payer Fee Schedule Setup",
      "body": "Please provide instructions on how to input and manage contracted fee schedules for new insurance payers. Additionally, we would appreciate clarification on whether updating these schedules will automatically affect any existing unbilled encounters currently in the system."
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-358",
      "subject": "Adding a new pharmacy to patient favorites",
      "body": "Hello, I just wanted to ask how we can look up a newly opened pharmacy in the directory and add it to a patient's preferred list. Thank you for your help!"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-359",
      "subject": "Waiting room check-in columns keep resetting",
      "body": "I am beyond frustrated with the waiting room queue display today. Every time I try to customize or rearrange the status columns to track arrival times better, the system reverts back to the default view after refreshing. Can someone please tell me how to make these column changes stick permanently so my front desk staff can actually do their jobs?"
    },
    {
      "id": "gen-360",
      "subject": "Troubleshooting electronic lab order rejections",
      "body": "Hello, I am writing to ask for a bit of assistance regarding some electronic lab orders that our reference laboratory recently bounced back. I tried looking at the requisition details, but I am not entirely sure how to properly attach the required ICD-10 diagnosis codes so the submission goes through smoothly next time. Sorry to trouble support with this, and thank you in advance for any guidance you can provide."
    }
  ]
}
